 "notes": "E371 is the same site as the unit (d=0) and N31 is the unit's Nigro entry (12 m): both coded grid (bearing invalid). SWP Beit Jubr et Tahtani (text names Cypros) is the place of Nigro N36 Beit Jabr et-Tahtani (Nigro cites Conder-Kitchener pp. 190-191): its birkeh 'immediately south of the fort' coded at grid N36; the fosse not recorded. SWP Tell es Sultan entry is not this unit and not within 2 km (no WBADB or Nigro entry for it within 2 km): ignored; its text is cut off mid-sentence. Not recorded: bath, columbarium tower, aqueducts, moat, ritual baths, rock shelters, niches, cliff, bare 'Site.' rows. Natural caves coded as pits. N1 'Pool Complex' coded pool yes because the source names it a pool complex."
